      "artist": "Robin Webster",
      "description": "\"Site of the original Edinburgh - Leith - Newhaven railway\", 1997An opening in the wall of Waverley station in line with this route, which was at right angles to the main line (which came later). Its terminal station was very short, and was largely built over by the northwards extension of Waverley station in the foreground, north of the old Canal Street. There was also a north to west connecting curve, joining the main line just to the west of the Waverley platforms. The terminal station closed to passengers in 1868.",
